{"meta":{"ticker":"VIG","as_of_date":"2026-06-22","performance_as_of":"2026-05-29","generated_at":"2026-06-23 10:47:22"},"benchmark":{"ticker":"SPY","fund_name":"State Street SPDR S&P 500 ETF"},"overview":{"ticker":"VIG","fund_name":"Vanguard Dividend Appreciation ETF","category":"US Large-Cap Value","issuer":"Vanguard","index_name":"S&P U.S. Dividend Growers Index","region":"North America","exchange":"NYSEARCA","expense_ratio":0.0004,"aum":107935765211,"holdings_count":341,"inception_date":"2006-04-21","overall_score":8.05186411894273,"overall_rank":179,"sector_diversification_score":5.95609583501819},"description":{"tsi_description":"VIG is a dividend growth ETF that focuses on U.S. companies with long records of consistently increasing dividend payments. The fund tracks the S&P U.S. Dividend Growers Index and emphasizes financially stable businesses capable of sustaining dividend growth over time. Unlike many higher-yield dividend ETFs, VIG intentionally excludes many ultra high-yield stocks and instead maintains meaningful exposure to lower-yielding companies with strong earnings growth and profitability characteristics. Its market-cap-weighted structure also results in meaningful allocations to large-cap technology and financial companies with established dividend growth histories. Overall, VIG offers a conservative and quality-focused approach to long-term dividend growth investing.","strategy_steps":["Tracks the S&P U.S. Dividend Growers Index.","Requires companies to have at least 10 consecutive years of dividend increases.","Excludes the highest-yielding 25% of eligible securities from the index universe.","Uses a market-capitalization weighting methodology.","Caps individual security weights at 4%.","Rebalances quarterly and reconstitutes annually.","Uses a passive indexing approach to replicate index performance."],"best_for":["Dividend growth","Long-term investing","Lower volatility"],"strengths":["Low turnover","Earnings growth","Dividend consistency"],